<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <LangVersion>default</LangVersion>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <Title>A lightweight, extensible, and attribute-driven Command Query Responsibility Segregation (CQRS) framework for .NET applications.</Title>
        <Authors>$(AssemblyName)</Authors>
        <Company>BisocM</Company>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/BisocM/CQRSharp</PackageProjectUrl>
        <PackageIcon>CQRSharp_Icon.png</PackageIcon>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/BisocM/CQRSharp</RepositoryUrl>
        <PackageTags>CQRS;</PackageTags>
        <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
        <Version>2.2.0</Version>
        <Description>A lightweight, extensible, and attribute-driven Command Query Responsibility Segregation (CQRS) framework for .NET applications.</Description>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>Modified NuGet-Compatible Release Notes for 2.2.0

Since NuGet does not support markdown formatting, you need to replace markdown elements with plain text formatting. Below is a revised version that should work properly on the NuGet page:

# Release Notes - Version 2.2.0  
Refactor Rate Limiting, Pipeline Configuration, and Code Cleanup  

 🚀 What's New in 2.2.0?  
This release introduces significant optimizations, refactors, and modular improvements to the system, focusing on rate limiting, pipeline configuration, and overall code clarity.

 🔧 Enhancements &amp; Optimizations  

Rate Limiting Enhancements:  
- Introduced periodic expiration for stale user/command pairs in _buckets, reducing memory usage.  
- Optimized bucket management logic for better efficiency and responsiveness.  

Dispatcher Refactor for DRY Compliance:  
- Removed redundant reflection in Dispatcher.  
- Introduced a centralized registry (RequestMetadata) that eagerly stores metadata, reducing computation overhead.  
- Improves performance and makes command execution more maintainable.  

Pipeline Configuration Refactor:  
- Separated DispatcherOptions into modular option classes:  
  - LoggingOptions  
  - TimeoutOptions  
  - ResilienceOptions  
- Added AddXBehavior extension methods for cleaner Dependency Injection (DI) pipeline behavior registration.  
- Updated existing implementations to use this new structure, improving readability and flexibility.  

Additional Improvements:
- Command Exemptions: Commands can now be exempted from multiple pipelines, offering more execution control.  
- General Code Cleanup: Improved readability, maintainability, and performance.  

📂 Breaking Changes?  
No major breaking changes—this version remains backward compatible while introducing a more modular and optimized architecture.  

⏭️ What’s Next?  
- Further enhancements to pipeline behaviors and command execution.  
- Additional performance and memory efficiency improvements.  </PackageReleaseNotes>
        <TargetFrameworks>net10.0;net8.0;net9.0</TargetFrameworks>
    </PropertyGroup>

